        {
            "status": "sourced",
            "value": "Nauka 13.1 x 4.25 m",
            "source": "Wikipedia 'Russian Orbital Station' (Dec 2025 plan): assembled at the ISS from Nauka + the Universal Node Module (UUM) + the Science-Power Module (NEM, on UUM's lower port) + the gateway airlock (ShM, side port), separated before the ISS deorbit; later a base module (an upgraded NEM) and two target modules (2033); 51.6 deg, ~400 km (was ~98 deg until Dec 2025); Nauka 13.1 m long, 4.25 m wide (Wikipedia 'Nauka'); RKK Energia NEM renders: two large wings at the aft end, side radiators",
            "subject": "ros_nauka"
        },
